# Hitstop only pauses the button buffer; hitstun is the fighter's own time and ages it. Testman's 5a hits p2 on
# frame 5: 8 hitstop frames (6-13), then hitstun until p2 is free on frame 27. A 5a p2 pressed in its hitstop
# (frame 10) is far older than the buffer by then, so it is no reversal: p2 just goes idle.
setup: p1 character testman
setup: p2 character testman
setup: p1 x = -30000
setup: p2 x = 30000

frame 1: p1 5a
frame 10: p2 5a

frame 5: expect p2 hitstop = 8
frame 26: expect p2 state = hitstun
frames 27-30: expect p2 state = idle
